Subject: [PATCH] draw: Loomy's Hy-Image generators draw on the images API
 (#4913)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iFlytek's Loomy gateway serves three image generators, each listed in
its /v1/models with type "image": Hy-Image-3.5-preview,
doubao-seedream-5-lite, qwen-image-3.0-pro. An OpenAI-compatible plugin
in front of it lists all three, and the reporter measured all three
answering a normal OpenAI-shaped draw on the images API with a 200 and
a URL each.

qwen-image and seedream match catalog.ImagesAPI's words, so those two
reach Settings' image generation picker and draw. hy-image matches only
DrawsID's "image", so Hy-Image-3.5-preview stayed a chat model with no
way to pick it for drawing — the same reason WorkBuddy's Hy-Image
models need their wbDrawers path.

Add "hy-image" to ImagesAPI's words: the model is then a drawer on the
plugin's row like the other two, and the gateway asks it on the images
API instead of chat. No other model's answer changes — every id the new
word catches was already a drawer by DrawsID's broader "image"; only
where it is asked moves.

Test: TestLoomyPluginDraws (internal/gateway) installs a fake Loomy
plugin listing the three generators beside a chat model, checks Drawers
lists all three, and draws Hy-Image-3.5-preview (images API, image
back, chat never asked). Broken by hand: without "hy-image" it is red
(drawers [doubao-seedream-5-lite qwen-image-3.0-pro], the Hy-Image one
missing).

